WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.060
Nine of twelve children met a trial's endpoint.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.100
Does that mean most of their hearing came back?

3
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:15.873
The DB-OTO trial treated twelve children with OTOF-related profound deafness.

4
00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:22.287
Nine met the week 24 endpoint: an average of 70 dB HL or better.

5
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:26.277
Three of twelve reached average normal sensitivity.

6
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.740
So nine of twelve is a share of children meeting an endpoint.

7
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.760
It is not a share of hearing.

8
00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:38.823
In a separate report by Wang and colleagues, one child's baseline was above the test

9
00:00:38.823 --> 00:00:40.803
ceiling of 95 dB.

10
00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:45.207
At week 26 the threshold was 58 dB.

11
00:00:46.027 --> 00:00:47.607
What does that tell you about the improvement?

12
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:56.517
Only that it was more than 37 dB.

13
00:00:57.277 --> 00:00:59.057
The true baseline was never measured.

14
00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:04.547
A floor on the improvement is not the improvement, and it is not a percentage of

15
00:01:04.547 --> 00:01:05.547
hearing.

16
00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.170
Now the harder case.

17
00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.410
When the hair cell itself is gone, putting back its gene cannot help.

18
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:16.590
A new hair cell has to be made, perhaps from a surviving supporting cell.

19
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.550
Birds replace damaged hair cells.

20
00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:24.210
In adult quail, counts recovered to within five percent of the original.

21
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.140
The adult mammalian cochlea does not do this.

22
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.500
One mammalian exception is vestibular, in the guinea-pig utricle.

23
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:41.300
In newborn mice, the factor ATOH1 pushes nonsensory cells of the cochlea, chiefly in

24
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.920
the greater epithelial ridge, toward hair cells.

25
00:01:44.983 --> 00:01:48.003
Would the same factor work just as well a week later?

26
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:56.503
By day eight, the factor alone gave very few new hair cells.

27
00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.263
Adding two more factors gave many more.

28
00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:06.087
Hair-cell genes also became less accessible with age.

29
00:02:06.967 --> 00:02:08.887
That makes chromatin a candidate barrier.

30
00:02:09.967 --> 00:02:13.927
In mature mice, some reprogrammed cells grew rudimentary bundles.

31
00:02:15.007 --> 00:02:17.227
Nerve fibres were reported to contact them.

32
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.320
Whether those contacts are working synapses is the unsettled step.

33
00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.100
Replacing a link in a surviving cell is being done in children.

34
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.260
Rebuilding the cell is not.
